Dear Rebecca, 

sorry for the late reply. To figure out if there are duplicated locations, can you try:
###
any(xyTable(x,y)$number > 1)
###
where x and y are your x/y coordinates? If the command replies TRUE, then chooseCN (called by spca) will think there are duplicated locations. To visualize them you can use the classical - and bit ugly - sunflowerplot:
###
sunflowerplot(x,y)
###
Red segments indicate duplicates.

The function xyTable rounds the coordinates up to a few digits before looking for duplicates. If you are entirely sure all your locations should be different, then we need to have chooseCN pass the right argument to xyTable when making the graph. This is easy to do but will require a little tweak of the function.

Cheers

Thibaut
